 "discussion": "SYNOPSIS\n\nThe benign weather pattern of the past few days will continue for at least two more as a ridge of high pressure remains firmly entrenched over the BC interior, bringing mainly sunny/clear skies, seasonally cool temperatures and light winds. Valley cloud/fog, if it should form, could keep temperatures a bit warmer than forecast. Freezing levels will continue to remain near village level during the afternoons.\n\nEXTENDED OUTLOOK\n\nFriday to Sunday: Cool, dry conditions will persist Friday and Saturday as the ridge of high pressure remains over the BC interior. The only discernible change will be the possibility of more cloud cover spilling into the area from storms passing by well south and north of the resort. On Sunday, a weak Pacific disturbance should bring increased cloud cover along with periods of light snow. Mid-mountain temperatures will be in the -4 to -6 °C range in the afternoons and -8 to -10 °C overnight, while village temperatures will likely range from zero to minus 2 in the afternoons and from -5 to - 8 °C overnight. Winds will continue to be light until Sunday when an increase in E to SE winds can be expected.",
